# Clone cache and downloaded ground-truth parquet/JSONL (rebuilt by fetch.py).
.clones/
.data/
.venv/

# Benchmark output: one JSONL per run — up to 23 MB each, 654 MB for a full
# tier-1 pass. Kept locally for comparison, never committed.
#
# What IS committed is the small end of the same pipeline: `published/` holds
# the aggregate summary and the paired-comparison output behind every number
# quoted in PROTOCOL.md or FINDINGS.md, plus a hash manifest of the query sets.
# `publish.py --check` fails if the two ever disagree. Without that directory
# nothing here could be verified without re-running the whole thing on a GPU.
results/

# The tier-0 replay fixture: a frozen SQLite file, a Qdrant snapshot and a
# query-vector cache. Large, binary, and regenerated by a tier-1 run.
fixtures/

__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Per-arm server configs written by slicer_sweep.py, and the corpora override
# that points a second server at its own clone. Both are derived from the
# committed originals by a one-line substitution the scripts perform.
.bench-config-*.toml
.corpora-*.toml
